.TH BUCHAREST\-LITE 1 "2026-10-14" "bucharest-lite 1.9.14" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bucharest\-lite \- open\-source non\-linear video editor (NLE)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bucharest\-lite
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Bucharest Lite
is a GPL\-3.0 licensed non\-linear video editor built on Qt6 and C++17, using
FFmpeg for media IO. It supports multi\-track timeline editing, keyframeable
clip properties, transitions, effects, color grading, chroma key compositing,
subtitle support and audio mixing.
.PP
Projects are saved as JSON files and can reference media by relative path.
Export supports the MP4, MKV and WebM containers with the H.264, VP9, AV1 and
AAC codecs.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/bucharest-lite/
User projects and autosaves. Autosaves are written every 60 seconds while a
project is dirty and on focus loss, keeping a rolling ring of ten; a newer
autosave than the last manual save is offered for recovery on next launch.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/bucharest-lite/plugins/
User\-installable codec plugins. A plugin here overrides the shipped copy of
the same name, so plugins can be updated without root.
.SH PLUGINS
Codec plugins are loaded dynamically at startup from the system directory and
then the user directory, each scanned for
.I video
and
.I audio
subdirectories. The system directory is
.IR /usr/lib/bucharest\-lite/plugins ,
resolved at build time from the install prefix, and carries the nine bundled
codecs (h264, vp9, av1, theora, mpeg4, aac, flac, vorbis, opus).
.PP
Each plugin exports
.BR bl_get_codec_plugin ()
and declares an ABI version; a plugin whose ABI does not match the host is
skipped with a log entry. Plugins are stateless factories: all state lives in
the context passed to them.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project README, FEATURES.md and docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE.md in the
source distribution.
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/wiczajac666/bucharestlite
.SH AUTHOR
BucharestLite contributors.